MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "All That Echoes feels like a natural next choice because Josh Groban's expressive singing connects directly with my interest in Stages and classical crossover.",
    "To Be Loved and Cheek to Cheek appeal to me through warm vocals, familiar standards, and polished singing that suit relaxed listening. Partners also fits my interest in vocal duets, although I would save it for another visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Pitch Perfect and Hamilton connect loosely with my interest in musical performances, but their energetic or rhythm-driven character does not match the relaxed, expressive singing I want now.",
    "That's Christmas To Me fits a past seasonal interest rather than my current mood, while The Blessed Unrest feels less connected to the orchestral and vocal music I am seeking. Neither listing titled 25 gives me enough information to judge its fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in theatrical singing seems to have been extended too broadly to soundtracks and cast recordings, even though their musical style matters to me.",
    "My earlier Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference, although I only want seasonal music at particular times."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent relaxing classical selection suggests that calm listening matters now, alongside my longer-standing interest in expressive vocal performances.",
    "The connection I value is the warmth of the voice, orchestral accompaniment, and style of singing; simply being another vocal album is not enough to make me choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in expressive singers but sometimes missed the relaxed mood and specific vocal styles that make an album appealing to me now."
}
